						<p>PROC R makes it easy to incorporate R code within SAS programs. Bu=
t what if you want to create an R script all on its own? Or, what if you wa=
nt to reference an external R script within your SAS program? Keep reading =
to find out how!</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>This is the third post in a series of posts introducing PROC R. If inter=
ested, parts 1 and 2 can be found here:</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Part 1:</strong> <a href=3D"https://communities.sas.com/t5/SAS-C=
ommunities-Library/Introducing-PROC-R-The-Newest-Way-to-Integrate-R-and-SAS=
-Part-1/ta-p/985832" target=3D"_blank">Introducing PROC R (Part 1): The New=
est Way to Integrate R and SAS</a></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Part 2: </strong><a href=3D"https://communities.sas.com/t5/SAS-C=
ommunities-Library/Introducing-PROC-R-The-Newest-Way-to-Integrate-R-and-SAS=
-Part-2/ta-p/988212" target=3D"_blank">Introducing PROC R (Part 2): Creatin=
g R Plots Within SAS Programs</a></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Part 4:&nbsp;</strong><a href=3D"https://communities.sas.com/t5/=
SAS-Communities-Library/Introducing-PROC-R-Part-4-Incorporating-R-Code-into=
-Flows-within/ta-p/992995" target=3D"_blank">Introducing PROC R (Part 4): I=
ncorporating R Code into Flows within SAS Data and AI Studio</a></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Note:</strong> To access PROC R, users should have access to SAS=
 Viya 2026.03 or later.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<h3 id=3D"toc-hId-1656785539">Creating a Stand-Alone R Script</h3>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>Embedding R code in a PROC R step is useful for quick analyses; however,=
 external R scripts are often preferred for larger projects, code reuse, an=
d collaboration. Within SAS Studio, users can create their own R scripts by=
 selecting <strong>Program in R</strong> from the Start page, or by selecti=
ng <strong>New</strong> &gt; <strong>R Program</strong>. This will create a=
 .R file where you can code exclusively in R without needing to specify the=
 PROC R step anywhere in the code.</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"text-align: center; color: #666; font-size: 80%;"><em><span cla=
ss=3D"lia-inline-image-display-wrapper lia-image-align-center" image-alt=3D=
"01_ST_Rprogramoptions.png" style=3D"width: 999px;"><span class=3D"lia-mess=
age-image-wrapper lia-message-image-actions-narrow lia-message-image-action=
s-below"><img src=3D"https://communities.sas.com/t5/image/serverpage/image-=
id/116113i3C519BB387EF4E2D/image-size/large?v=3Dv2&amp;px=3D999" role=3D"bu=
tton" title=3D"01_ST_Rprogramoptions.png" alt=3D"01_ST_Rprogramoptions.png"=
 li-image-url=3D"https://communities.sas.com/t5/image/serverpage/image-id/1=
16113i3C519BB387EF4E2D?v=3Dv2" li-image-display-id=3D"'116113i3C519BB387EF4=
E2D'" li-message-uid=3D"'990279'" li-messages-message-image=3D"true" li-bin=
dable=3D"" class=3D"lia-media-image" tabindex=3D"0" li-bypass-lightbox-when=
-linked=3D"true" li-use-hover-links=3D"false" li-compiled=3D"true"><!----><=
/span></span></em></p>
<p style=3D"text-align: center; color: #666; font-size: 80%;"><em>Select an=
y image to see a larger version.</em><br><em>Mobile users: To view the imag=
es, select the "Full" version at the bottom of the page.</em></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>For example, the following R code analyzes the SASHELP.CARS data set, pr=
oducing a histogram of highway miles per gallon and a table of information =
for Honda vehicles:</p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<pre class=3D"  language-sas"><code class=3D"  language-sas"><span class=3D=
"token function keyword">library</span><span class=3D"token punctuation">(<=
/span>tidyverse<span class=3D"token punctuation">)</span>

VMake <span class=3D"token operator">&lt;</span><span class=3D"token operat=
or">-</span> <span class=3D"token string">"Honda"</span>
carsdf <span class=3D"token operator">&lt;</span><span class=3D"token opera=
tor">-</span> <span class=3D"token function keyword">sd2df</span><span clas=
s=3D"token punctuation">(</span><span class=3D"token string">"sashelp.cars"=
</span><span class=3D"token punctuation">)</span>

mycars <span class=3D"token operator">&lt;</span><span class=3D"token opera=
tor">-</span> carsdf <span class=3D"token punctuation">%</span><span class=
=3D"token operator">&gt;</span><span class=3D"token punctuation">%</span>
<span class=3D"token function keyword">filter</span><span class=3D"token pu=
nctuation">(</span>Make <span class=3D"token operator">=3D</span><span clas=
s=3D"token operator">=3D</span> VMake<span class=3D"token punctuation">)</s=
